    {
      "id": "antony-and-cleopatra/sceneIV_3.8/p@165252",
      "type": "passage",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "[To Scarus.] Give me thy hand.\nTo this great fairy I’ll commend thy acts,\nMake her thanks bless thee. O thou day o’ th’ world,\nChain mine armed neck. Leap thou, attire and all,\nThrough proof of harness to my heart, and there\nRide on the pants triumphing.",
